@page page_third-party_performance_analysis_tools Performance analysis tools


<!-- Add this one for href links to subitems -->
\tableofcontents

Peano provides bespoke support for some external performance analysis tools.


# ScoreP


## Compilation

When using ScoreP the configure or cmake command should be prefixed with SCOREP_WRAPPER=off,
and the compiler names should be prefixed with scorep-. For an Intel toolchain
with autotools this looks like:

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
SCOREP_WRAPPER=off ./configure CC=scorep-icx CXX=scorep-icpx ...
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

<br /><br />
<div style="background-color: #fcc ; padding: 10px; border: 1px solid green;"> 
The instruction above assumes that Score-P's module files are built such that 
they provide scripts alike scorep-icx. 
</div>


If you compile without switching the instrumentation off, Score-P will 
instrument every single element of all Peano libraries which will be extremely
excessive. 

## Logging

Peano provides bespoke logging for Score-P. Indeed, it it not a good idea to 
use Peano with its default @ref tarch_logging "command line logger". This 
logger does indentation and fancy string formatting, and all of these things
draw compute resources which pollute your profile. You don't need them and it
is way more efficient to use the @ref tarch_logging "Score-P logger" that is 
shipped with the code. 

In summary, I recommend to add

~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
SCOREP_WRAPPER=off ./configure CC=scorep-icx CXX=scorep-icpx ... --with-toolchain=scorep
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

to the configuration.



# MAQAO

When using any performance analysis tool the compilation flag "-g" should be
used, to generate debug information. For MAQAO this may not be sufficient, in 
which case "-grecord-gcc-switches" should also be used.

MAQAO reports can be generated on login nodes using
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
maqao oneview -R1 -- ./program
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
or on compute nodes using
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
maqao oneview -R1 --mpi-command="srun -p <partition_name> -A <account> -t <time>" -- ./program
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
Find a reference guide at https://www.maqao.org/documentation/MAQAO_QuickReferenceSheet.pdf

*/